# Task12 separate metadata-only final package acceptance boundary

Task12 Ruling: [68] Keep the frozen raw translation manifest and independent pair diagnostic as non-acceptance identity/transport records, and add ONE separate owned, prearchived, metadata-only final package acceptance boundary instead of changing frozen native/runtime/catalog inputs. Named local inspection of task-12-package.py:55-60 and task-12-package-verify.py:12-36 confirms exact version/mode/errornull/four-pinned-reference/raw-original-archive/Git/audit-unchanged checks exist, but these raw records have no fixed requiredFinalFlags/failedFinalFlags qualification list. They must never themselves be presented as catalog/behavior/source-ready acceptance. Authorize only a uniquely owned ignored Task12 binder, its pure portable synthetic-negative tests and actual invocation/output/exit receipt, all scripts and fixture inputs archived before execution and later retained as exact hashed evidence. Do not edit the frozen package/diagnostic scripts, migration90d, any native executed driver/reader/codec/profile/renderer/validator, existing acceptance predicates, shared scanner, audit source/attributes/exclusions or historical artifacts. The new acceptance wrapper must independently compute its checks from actual raw originals/archives/current source/read-only Git identities and receipt-type-specific fixed contracts; never promote an input's self-declared verified/count/flag value. Require exact typed version/mode/counts, errornull/failedFinalFlags[], a fixed literal-TRUE requiredFinalFlags set, all immutable source/current/Git/original/archive raw+canonical+Git+byte pairs, exactly the R66 four pinned accepted-base references and no new Task11 payload, unchanged audit/Task11 source, complete current source freeze, R67's exact qualified208-native/de35-supporting-test bridge, three actual current-source composition receipts, all mandated local gate invocation/exit evidence, and complete current ordered original ruling texts. If an input is missing/mismatched/unexecuted, a required literal flag is missing/false, profile/cardinality/context differs, raw/git/content/reference identity differs, or an actual gate failed, reject with nonzero after retaining an error/failed-flags receipt. Portable negatives must exercise these actual validator branches with synthetic files, not merely assert constants or provide acceptance flags. Native208's22-flag receipt and source/raw semantics remain unchanged and qualified; do not relabel it as current full native Bun coverage. Newly created metadata binder/fixture bytes are not native executions or DB profile changes and must not cause a DB rerun merely to archive them. Final closing Git binding and actual fresh five-job/non-skipped PG17.11 group CI remain separate mandatory controller gates; this pre-closing package qualifier cannot claim those pending gates or production/deployment/operational readiness. Preserve original raw manifests, original diagnostic behavior, actual rejected R65, original failed captures/hosted/prelaunch/move/RED proofs, all67 prior ordered texts and final68 originals. Before final acceptance, root independently binds the actual new binder/source/tests/invocation/receipt and complete closing Git originals-to-archives, and the fresh task reviewer judges this new boundary on its merits without pre-graded severity. If this concrete bounded action is itself automatically rejected, retain the reason and stop that action; do not retry an equivalent predicate change or another waiver. Reason: transport manifests prove byte identities while explicit readiness requires stronger fixed evidence qualification; a separate fail-closed metadata boundary adds that qualification without altering code and native tests already executed on frozen inputs. Cost if wrong: classifying a readiness consumer as mere transport, trusting claimed booleans/counts, accepting incomplete provenance, or changing executed source underneath old proofs could make invalid evidence appear ready; require independently computed fixed contracts, meaningful negatives, original-byte preservation, root Git closure and fresh review/CI with honest pending/not-run labels. This adds no source ACL/audit/scanner exception, production/main/release/provider/payment/email/refund/publication/schedule/paid-branch authority.
